---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Cookie Policy | KawaiiPlay';
const description = 'Learn how KawaiiPlay and its advertising partners use cookies and local storage.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/cookie-policy/">
  <main class="container">
    <article class="content-page">
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated-note">Last updated: January 2026</p>

      <p>This Cookie Policy explains how KawaiiPlay ("we") uses cookies and similar technologies (such as browser local storage) when you visit ubg2028.github.io.</p>

      <h2>1. What Are Cookies?</h2>
      <p>Cookies are small text files placed on your device by websites you visit. They are widely used to make websites function, remember preferences, and deliver relevant advertising.</p>

      <h2>2. Types of Cookies & Storage We Use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Essential/Functional:</strong> remembers your dark/light theme preference.</li>
        <li><strong>Local storage (not a cookie, but similar purpose):</strong> powers on-site features like Favorites, Recently Played, daily play streaks, and star ratings — kept entirely on your device.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising cookies:</strong> set by third-party ad networks (including Google AdSense) to serve and measure ads, and in some cases to personalize ads based on your browsing activity.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics cookies:</strong> may be used to understand aggregate traffic and usage patterns.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Third-Party Cookies</h2>
      <p>Google and its partners may use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to this and other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads to users. You can opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>

      <h2>4. Managing Cookies</h2>
      <p>Most web browsers let you control cookies through their settings, including blocking or deleting them. Note that disabling cookies may affect the functionality of some parts of the Site. You can also clear locally stored Favorites/Recently-Played data at any time by clearing your browser's site data for ubg2028.github.io.</p>

      <h2>5. Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Cookie Policy periodically. Continued use of the Site after changes means you accept the updated policy.</p>

      <h2>6. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Visit our <a href="/contact-us/">Contact Us</a> page.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
